 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Hair dye: the semi-permanent SKU list was cut from 10 to a list of the brands that cover the market, plus the Good Housekeeping at-home test picks (Phytocolor, Revlon ColorSilk, eSalon, Madison Reed). I dropped the Adore, Joico, Keratin Complex, Milkshake, Osmo and Pravana SKUs. They are salon/retailer SKUs with no archetype. Madison Reed's root touch-up was folded into the types. Ten archetypes, ordered by history: Poly Color, Miss Clairol, Nice'n Easy, Préférence, Excellence, Koleston, Igora Royal, Manic Panic, Lush Henna, Natural Instincts. The L'Oréal brand founding year was left blank because no retrieved page confirmed it. Préférence's exact launch year is not confirmed; the date comes from the 1971 slogan and 1973 TV spot. Wigs: lace front and full lace are maker-free archetypes; Raquel Welch (HairUWear) and Jon Renau were confirmed from their own pages. The claim that they lead the market was not confirmed independently. Hairpiece: the Hairdo toppers were merged into one line. Toupée and extensions were added as maker-free archetypes. No traditions were added: the henna tradition belongs on the Traditional adornment shelf. The Wikidata and Wikipedia helper tools failed in this session, so sources were fetched directly.",
